  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies projected quantum features built from a Heisenberg feature map and XGBoost for credit default prediction. On balanced data, the quantum models reach 86.4% test accuracy on a 20-qubit statevector run and 87.7%/88.9%/88.8% on IBM hardware (ibm_brisbane/ibm_torino/ibm_marrakesh), while the corresponding classical baselines are 89.10%, 88.7%, 89.8%, and 89.6%. On unbalanced 10,000-sample data, the best reported CDR is 0.8013 on the MPS simulator and 0.8000 on IBM hardware via ensemble methods, slightly above the classical baselines but not a standalone quantum advantage.",
